OL,3,AWhite House pulls Tetris-style 'Build
OL,4,AThe Wall' game after copyright concern
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe White House has taken down a
OL,7,FTetris-style game on its website called
OL,8,F"Build The Wall", days after The Tetris
OL,9,FCompany raised concerns over its use of
OL,10,Fthe game's likeness.
OL,12,FThe game, which saw players stack
OL,13,Fblocks to build a wall to "protect the
OL,14,Fborder" is one of five arcade games
OL,15,Fwhich have appeared on the White House
OL,16,Fwebsite.
OL,18,FOn 4 September the official Tetris
OL,19,Faccount on X posted the firm was "not
OL,20,Finvolved in the creation" of the game
OL,21,Fand it took "copyright infringement
OL,22,Fvery seriously".
OL,23,APub: 09-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG7/19
OL,24,ANext PageBTechnologyC Nat RadioFCulture
